WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/admin/components/security-access/LiveVehicleState.tsx — a presentational leaf fed by its
  parent's security-latest query (prop `latest: SecurityEvent | undefined`):
    FadeIn(0.17) → GlassPanel(p-4) → header[ h2 "Live Vehicle State"
                                              + {latest && <Live/>}  (CircleDot animate-pulse, text-green-400) ]
                                   → liveSignals.length > 0
                                        ? grid(2 / sm:3 / lg:5) of GlassPanel cells
                                        : <EmptyState message="No live state data available" />
  `buildLiveSignals(ev)` returns [] when `ev` is undefined (→ EmptyState), else TEN cells:
    hazards · highBeams · turnSignal · driverSeat · pairedKeys · valetMode · serviceMode · speedLimit ·
    homelinkDevices · centerDisplay.
  Each cell = { label, icon, value, active }. Value builders:
    boolLabel(b)           : null → '—' · true → On · false → Off          (hazards/highBeams/valet/service)
    asNonEmptyString(s)??'—' (turnSignal/centerDisplay)                     · active = !!s && !s.lower.includes('off')
    driverSeat             : null → '—' · true → Occupied · false → Empty   · active = !!occupied
    pairedKeys/homelink    : count!=null ? String(count) : '—'             · active = (count ?? 0) > 0
    speedLimit             : typeof boolean ? On/Off : asNonEmptyString??'—' · active = boolean ? flag : strRule
  active cell ⇒ icon text-cyan-400 + value text-white; inactive ⇒ text-muted. No loading/error/stale/offline in
  the web leaf (the parent query owns those) — reproduced natively per the HIG states contract.

